The Reclusive Law of Inherent Paradox (RLIP) has evolved from the Recursive Law of Inverse Pressure which has been mentioned in various of my earlier works.

The Reclusive Law of Inherent Paradox states that contradiction density over time inversely drives recursive pressure, causing structural reorganization as contradictions increase. It is mathematically expressed as (P_{r}(t) = -\frac{dC(t)}{dt}), where (P_{r}(t)) is recursive pressure and (C(t)) is contradiction density.